            <note corresp="#d28-f2" n="2" xml:id="d28-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg872">p. 872</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d28-f3" n="3" xml:id="d28-f3-content">
                <p>Brackets in the source text.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d28-f4" n="4" xml:id="d28-f4-content">
                <p>In his reply of June 18, Hickerson
                    first briefly reviewed the contents of Dean’s letter, then added: “As you are doubtless aware, this
                    matter is being studied and a paper is being prepared through the Executive
                    Committee on Regulation of Armaments (RAC).
                    Members of the staff of the Atomic Energy Commission are participating actively
                    in this study.” (103 AEC/5–2352)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
